# GitHub Pages Deployment Notes

## To deploy to GitHub Pages:

### Option 1: Automatic Deployment (Recommended)
1. Make sure you have a GitHub repository set up
2. Push your code to the main branch
3. The GitHub Actions workflow (.github/workflows/deploy.yml) will automatically:
   - Build your project
   - Deploy it to GitHub Pages
4. Go to Settings → Pages in your GitHub repo
5. Select "GitHub Actions" as the deployment source
6. Your site will be available at: https://yourusername.github.io/kanban-board/

### Option 2: Manual Deployment
```bash
npm run deploy
```

This command:
1. Builds the project
2. Commits the dist folder
3. Pushes to gh-pages branch
4. GitHub Pages will automatically serve the latest version

## Important Notes:
- The `base` in vite.config.ts is set to '/kanban-board/' - change this if your repo name is different
- Make sure GitHub Pages is enabled in your repository settings
- Select "GitHub Actions" as the source (not "Deploy from a branch")
